  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Low clouds and fog lingering into this morning.\n\nCoastal low will continue to weaken and exit east today. Lingering\nlow level moisture will maintain low stratus and areas of fog this\nmorning. The lowest visibilities are expected across the\nhilltops, with an outside chance for drizzle patches. Drier air\npushing southward will eroding the low clouds and fog from \nnorth to south today, with clouds across the inland Southern \nTier fading last by this evening. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Warming trend mid-week ahead of the next rain shower \nbearing cold front.\n\nDeveloping southerly flow by midweek will send a warm autumn airmass\ninto our region. Ridging aloft and 850 mb temperatures rising into\nthe upper teens C will aid in surface temperatures warming some 10\ndegrees above normal, with Thursday the likely the warmest day.\nA few sites, especially in the Genesee Valley/western Finger\nLakes, will make a run at 80F on Thursday.",
